Z||000000||KRMFiero||07-09-2001||05:42 PM||||Okay I found a Fiero down the street from me here are some pictures:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pic_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pic_5.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pic_6.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pic_2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pic_4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pic_3.jpg"> <P>Body Panels need paint but no deep scraches, needs a windshield, needs a Cylinder head (Yes it is a Duke, Automatic - He said it is a 86), The Interier is in desent Condition - It has Power windows and Locks, seats dont appear to be ripped but there are boxes on seats so im not sure, How much should I offer him? I belive it has been sitting for over a year, I will talk to him again tonight and try to get the VIN off if someone can run a CARFAX for me<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>       <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> <BR>AOL: Physcokyle||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-09-2001||05:51 PM||||IMHO, don't offer more than a couple hundred. 4 cyl autos are very common and since it needs body and engine work, you should be able to get it for very cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||07-09-2001||07:11 PM||||Heres how I estimate a price. Really look the car over and see how many good reasonable parts there on it. Like you were gonna part it out. Then offer about 2/3 of what you think the parts alone are worth. That way if you cant get it streetable you can recoupe your money by parting it out.<P>Thats how I kind of look at it.<P>I would offer MAX, MAX $350.<BR>But then its hard to tell by looking at just the pics.<P>Hope this helps.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
